WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.367
-How you been? How's the family?
How's everybody doing?

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:04.534
-Everybody's great.

00:00:04.534 --> 00:00:05.601
I just had a new niece
a couple months ago.

00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:06.767
-Hey!
-So, she's the fifth one.

00:00:06.767 --> 00:00:07.834
Very excited.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.834 --> 00:00:09.234
-Congratulations.
-Thank you.

00:00:09.234 --> 00:00:13.234
I'm proud of Auntie, which
I got to make this confession.

00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:15.033
-Ooh!
-Can I tell y'all?

00:00:15.033 --> 00:00:16.367
Have y'all had, like --
They have, like,

00:00:16.367 --> 00:00:20.133
these popcorn things
at the daycare at school

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:21.968
where, like, the kids
have to sell popcorn?

00:00:21.968 --> 00:00:24.100
-Uh-huh.
-Have you heard of that?

00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:27.901
Anyway, they had one at --
My nephew, he's like 4.

00:00:27.901 --> 00:00:28.934
He just turned 5.

00:00:28.934 --> 00:00:30.634
And my sister hits up
and is like,

00:00:30.634 --> 00:00:34.801
"Oh, they're selling popcorn
at the school.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:37.000
The kids are competing
against each other.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.834
And I just --
I really want him to win."

00:00:38.834 --> 00:00:41.767
And my sister
doesn't ask for anything.

00:00:41.767 --> 00:00:42.934
So I'm like, "Yeah, bet."

00:00:42.934 --> 00:00:44.234
So she was like,
"Can you just tell your friends,

00:00:44.234 --> 00:00:46.267
'Here's a link to buy
some popcorn'?"

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:47.868
And I was like, "Easy."
And I do it.

00:00:47.868 --> 00:00:49.033
And then she's like,
"Can you also, like,

00:00:49.033 --> 00:00:51.467
tell your company,
your employees?"

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:53.100
And I was like,
"I don't want to do that,

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.334
because then they'll feel
obligated to buy it."

00:00:55.334 --> 00:00:59.067
But then I was like,
I have to pick up the slack.

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:01.701
You know, like I have
to make sure that he wins,

00:01:01.701 --> 00:01:04.501
so I'm going to buy
a bunch of popcorn

00:01:04.501 --> 00:01:05.634
to get him to number one."

00:01:05.634 --> 00:01:06.901
-That's correct.

00:01:06.901 --> 00:01:08.801
-And, so,
my older brother is, like,

00:01:08.801 --> 00:01:10.367
obsessing over the game, too,

00:01:10.367 --> 00:01:12.167
and he's, like,
targeting this one kid

00:01:12.167 --> 00:01:13.601
who's actually in first place.

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:15.834
And I'll name him --
-This is 4 years old?

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:18.400
-He's --
They're literally 4 years old.

00:01:18.400 --> 00:01:20.467
And I'll call him, like,
Zulu or something.

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:23.467
And, so, Zulu --
He's like, "Oh, Zulu.

00:01:23.467 --> 00:01:25.901
Zulu is so smug and he thinks
he's going to take this,

00:01:25.901 --> 00:01:27.400
like, first-place prize."

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:28.968
And I'm like,
"Uh, guys, they're kids.

00:01:28.968 --> 00:01:30.167
Like, let's chill."

00:01:30.167 --> 00:01:32.968
But I'm getting
the competitive spirit, too.

00:01:32.968 --> 00:01:37.934
So, like, I spend a lot of money
on this popcorn, and --

00:01:37.934 --> 00:01:39.000
-You don't need
this much popcorn.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:40.167
You're doing this for your --

00:01:40.167 --> 00:01:41.467
-I don't need --
Yeah, I just want him to win.

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:43.734
She asked for it.
So, he gets to number one.

00:01:43.734 --> 00:01:45.901
And then, at the deadline,
it's, like, where --

00:01:45.901 --> 00:01:47.667
It's like 4:50.

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:49.200
And I'm like,
"I know one of these parents --

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.467
they're gonna, like --
they're going to try to,

00:01:50.467 --> 00:01:51.968
like, get their kid up.

00:01:51.968 --> 00:01:56.934
So at 4:59 on the dot, I'm going
to just boost it a little bit."

00:01:56.934 --> 00:01:59.033
-That's what I'm talking -- Yep.
That's exactly.

00:01:59.033 --> 00:02:01.334
Just goose it a little bit.
-You have to do that.

00:02:01.334 --> 00:02:04.067
-You got to.
-So, like, I set it all up.

00:02:04.067 --> 00:02:06.167
I put a little extra money
on there

00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:11.434
and I hit the "purchase" button
right at 4:59.59.

00:02:11.434 --> 00:02:12.634
-Yes.

00:02:12.634 --> 00:02:16.601
-And then I realized
I gave it to Zulu.

00:02:16.601 --> 00:02:20.534
And Zulu was in first place!

00:02:20.534 --> 00:02:23.968
So the family group chat
is going crazy.

00:02:23.968 --> 00:02:26.367
They're just like,
"How could this happen?

00:02:26.367 --> 00:02:29.100
Parents are so greedy.
People take this too seriously."

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:31.133
And I'm dead silent.

00:02:31.133 --> 00:02:33.434
-Does anyone in your family
know that it was you?

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:36.701
-So, I was calling
American Express like,

00:02:36.701 --> 00:02:38.834
"Please, can we --
can we cancel?

00:02:38.834 --> 00:02:41.133
Like, this is fraud."

00:02:41.133 --> 00:02:48.234
And, so, it wasn't until the
next day where they were like,

00:02:48.234 --> 00:02:52.267
"Oh, you can cancel it"
that, you know, then I --

00:02:52.267 --> 00:02:54.634
then I decided --
Then he got, like, second place.

00:02:54.634 --> 00:02:58.434
But sorry to Zulu.
He dropped down in the numbers.

00:02:58.434 --> 00:03:01.534
-Wait. So Zulu ended up not
getting the champion?

00:03:01.534 --> 00:03:03.300
-Well, because I put
him over the edge,

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:04.934
so I wasn't about
to do my nephew like that.

00:03:04.934 --> 00:03:09.534
Like, you know, technically,
my nephew won fair and square.

00:03:09.534 --> 00:03:11.367
-He did not win fair and square.

00:03:11.367 --> 00:03:13.167
This is a terrible lesson.
-You know what's crazy?

00:03:13.167 --> 00:03:15.033
-Terrible lesson
to teach your nephew.

00:03:15.033 --> 00:03:16.868
-He didn't even care.

00:03:16.868 --> 00:03:20.300
Like, my sister was like,
"You got second place,"

00:03:20.300 --> 00:03:22.901
and he was like, "Oh, okay."

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:23.968
-Yeah.
-Had no concerns.

00:03:23.968 --> 00:03:25.133
-Yeah,
I remember that whole thing.

00:03:25.133 --> 00:03:26.801
I had to sell chocolate bars
when I was a kid.

00:03:26.801 --> 00:03:29.200
And I remember doing it
for a Girl Scout cookies, too,

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:31.567
because I support
the Girl Scouts all the time.

00:03:31.567 --> 00:03:33.200
And I went to this one store

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:36.033
and I saw this girl
was selling Girl Scout cookies.

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:37.501
I go -- I went up to her.

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:39.200
I go, "I'm buying
everything you got.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.000
Give me everything.
I'm buying it."

00:03:41.000 --> 00:03:45.734
And she didn't care.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:45.734 --> 00:03:47.767
And then the mom
was kind of bummed, too.

00:03:47.767 --> 00:03:49.601
And I go --
And then I'm thinking,

00:03:49.601 --> 00:03:51.234
"Well, maybe the mom is bummed
because she's like,

00:03:51.234 --> 00:03:55.000
'Look, I've been out here for
eight hours with my daughter,

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:58.467
and some strange man comes over,
saves the day?

00:03:58.467 --> 00:04:01.167
Yeah, why don't -- You know,
this is ridiculous.

00:04:01.167 --> 00:04:03.033
I put the work in.
Let her earn it.'"

00:04:03.033 --> 00:04:05.167
-Let her earn it.
-Butt out, Jimmy Fallon.

00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:07.601
Butt out and let
my daughter grow up

00:04:07.601 --> 00:04:09.167
and figure out business.

00:04:09.167 --> 00:04:11.434
-Listen, if someone had come
to me and just bought it --

00:04:11.434 --> 00:04:13.167
Because it's so hard
to just be out there

00:04:13.167 --> 00:04:14.167
selling boxes.

00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:15.767
I would happily.

00:04:15.767 --> 00:04:18.100
I wish you were around
when I was a kid.

00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:19.334
-Really?

00:04:19.334 --> 00:04:20.968
-Because I gave up
selling Girl Scout cookies.

00:04:20.968 --> 00:04:23.300
Honestly, it was just --
It was -- I would eat them.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:27.234
-You just eat what
you're supposed to sell?

00:04:27.234 --> 00:04:28.734
-Yes, pretty much.
-Yeah.

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:31.534
-I mean, you can't trust a girl
who likes to eat with cookies.

00:04:31.534 --> 00:04:34.133
So...sorry. Shout-out to --

00:04:34.133 --> 00:04:35.801
-What's your favorite
Girl Scout cookie?

00:04:35.801 --> 00:04:38.767
-I loved Thin Mints
growing up, which is dis--

00:04:38.767 --> 00:04:39.968
But --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:39.968 --> 00:04:42.567
Y'all still like 'em?
Then I love them, too.

00:04:42.567 --> 00:04:46.567
But now I'm a -- What's the one
with the peanut butter?

00:04:46.567 --> 00:04:49.734
Tagalongs. I love Tagalongs.
And you freeze them and --

00:04:49.734 --> 00:04:51.200
-No, freezing is
the whole new thing now.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:54.200
Any cookie, the girls -- They
go, "Did you try them frozen?"

00:04:54.200 --> 00:04:55.868
-Yeah, Thin Mints
are really good frozen.

00:04:55.868 --> 00:04:57.200
-Amazing frozen.
-Yeah.

00:04:57.200 --> 00:04:59.300
-What's the one
with the coconut in them?

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:01.634
-Coconut?
-Samoas?

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:02.868
They're the best.

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:04.133
-I don't think they --
Yeah, kids shouldn't --

00:05:04.133 --> 00:05:06.234
[ Audience cheers ]
-No, Samoas with coconut?

00:05:06.234 --> 00:05:08.367
For kids?
Kids do not like coconut.

00:05:08.367 --> 00:05:09.868
Remember you have
the box of chocolates,

00:05:09.868 --> 00:05:11.834
and then you'd eat one
that had coconut inside

00:05:11.834 --> 00:05:14.200
and it felt like a violation?

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:18.100
-No. Violation was like
an orange cream or something.

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:20.901
[ Laughter ]
It would bum me out.

00:05:20.901 --> 00:05:22.934
It would bum me out,
orange cream.

00:05:22.934 --> 00:05:24.534
-That's so real. Or cherry.

00:05:24.534 --> 00:05:25.801
My grandmother would
buy, like,

00:05:25.801 --> 00:05:27.901
chocolate-covered cherries,
and they were gooey,

00:05:27.901 --> 00:05:31.767
so it was like just
cherry spit in your mouth.

00:05:33.701 --> 00:05:36.467
-I have things that I
want to talk to you about.

00:05:36.467 --> 00:05:40.067
One is I know you have
your own record label,

00:05:40.067 --> 00:05:41.067
called Raedio.

00:05:41.067 --> 00:05:43.834
-Yes. Yes, yes, yes.

00:05:43.834 --> 00:05:45.801
-I also want to
congratulate you on

00:05:45.801 --> 00:05:47.868
not one, but two Peabody Awards.

00:05:47.868 --> 00:05:49.334
You're a --
-Thank you.

00:05:49.334 --> 00:05:50.834
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:05:50.834 --> 00:05:54.501
Two. You won two Peabody Awards.
-Yes.

00:05:54.501 --> 00:05:56.300
-I mean, does that --
How does that feel?

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:58.267
-I mean, it feels amazing.

00:05:58.267 --> 00:05:59.934
So, the second one is, like --

00:05:59.934 --> 00:06:01.501
We were supposed to have,
like, a ceremony,

00:06:01.501 --> 00:06:02.834
and I was super-excited
about it.

00:06:02.834 --> 00:06:05.067
But, you know,
the ceremony got canceled

00:06:05.067 --> 00:06:07.100
due to the strikes,
which I support.

00:06:07.100 --> 00:06:09.667
So, they haven't --
I don't have the awards yet.

00:06:09.667 --> 00:06:12.200
So maybe talking about it on TV,
they'll send it.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:13.601
But I'm super-grateful.

00:06:13.601 --> 00:06:15.868
-Yeah, you got to take your
little victory lap. Come on.

00:06:15.868 --> 00:06:17.701
-Yeah, so, they gave me
a Trailblazer one.

00:06:17.701 --> 00:06:20.901
And it's with Lily Tomlin,
who is, like, such an icon.

00:06:20.901 --> 00:06:22.934
-Yeah, she is.
She's the greatest.

00:06:22.934 --> 00:06:25.300
-I hope we still get to have --
-But you are a trailblazer.

00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:27.767
-Thank you. Thank you.
-I have a photo of you.

00:06:27.767 --> 00:06:29.467
Look at this little --
This is baby Issa.

00:06:29.467 --> 00:06:31.300
[ Audience "Awws" ]
Look at that.

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:32.634
-Thank you for that "aww," guys.

00:06:32.634 --> 00:06:35.901
-This is a double
Peabody Award-winning producer,

00:06:35.901 --> 00:06:37.334
writer, comedian, actor.

00:06:37.334 --> 00:06:39.667
I mean, you do it all.
-I try. Thank you.

00:06:39.667 --> 00:06:42.801
-Yeah, you do it all.
-Thank you so much.

00:06:42.801 --> 00:06:47.968
-And you also have a
show called "Rap..."

00:06:47.968 --> 00:06:49.801
-Bleep!
-Yes. S-blank.

00:06:49.801 --> 00:06:50.934
-"Rap S."

00:06:50.934 --> 00:06:52.767
-"Rap --" Yeah.
-"Stuff."

00:06:52.767 --> 00:06:55.200
-Yeah, "Rap Stuff."
-Yes. Yes.

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:57.334
It's entering its second season.

00:06:57.334 --> 00:07:03.133
It's a show on Max about
two aspiring female rappers.

00:07:03.133 --> 00:07:04.868
And it really -- It talks
about the music industry.

00:07:04.868 --> 00:07:07.100
For those of you
who follow, like --

00:07:07.100 --> 00:07:10.000
Female rappers are having
a big moment in rap right now.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.634
They're being --
They're the most innovative.

00:07:11.634 --> 00:07:13.901
And this -- You know,
the second season is --

00:07:13.901 --> 00:07:15.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:15.334 --> 00:07:17.133
And we take a lot of
real-life inspiration,

00:07:17.133 --> 00:07:18.200
but it's a comedy.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:19.934
And this season,
the girls kill it.

00:07:19.934 --> 00:07:22.234
It's so good,
so watch it November 9th.

00:07:22.234 --> 00:07:24.601
-Yeah, November 9th.
I'm happy for you.

00:07:24.601 --> 00:07:25.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:25.968 --> 00:07:30.067
Then here we go into Viarae.
Talk to me about prosecco.

00:07:30.067 --> 00:07:31.567
How did you get involved
with prosecco?

00:07:31.567 --> 00:07:33.868
-I love prosecco.
Have y'all had prosecco before?

00:07:33.868 --> 00:07:35.100
[ Audience cheers ]

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:37.100
So, prosecco, to me,
like, it's --

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:40.467
I was introduced to it
right before we shot the pilot

00:07:40.467 --> 00:07:42.000
for my show "Insecure."

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:44.267
I had a director --
Our director,

00:07:44.267 --> 00:07:45.734
our pilot director,
Melina Matsoukas --

00:07:45.734 --> 00:07:47.734
we had, like, a
getting-to-know-you dinner

00:07:47.734 --> 00:07:49.033
before we shot.

00:07:49.033 --> 00:07:53.367
And she orders prosecco,
and I'm like, "What is that?"

00:07:53.367 --> 00:07:54.701
And she was like, "You'll see."

00:07:54.701 --> 00:07:58.167
And I loved it
because I wasn't at the place

00:07:58.167 --> 00:07:59.968
where I could, like,
pop champagne

00:07:59.968 --> 00:08:01.801
because I just wasn't
able to, like,

00:08:01.801 --> 00:08:03.033
afford champagne like that.

00:08:03.033 --> 00:08:06.834
But prosecco felt, like,
approachably luxurious.

00:08:06.834 --> 00:08:08.400
And since then,
it's just been, like,

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:10.334
my milestone drink
to celebrate friends.

00:08:10.334 --> 00:08:12.968
It's, like,
all the best moments I've had,

00:08:12.968 --> 00:08:15.701
a prosecco glass
has been in my hand.

00:08:15.701 --> 00:08:17.734
And so I was like, "Oh --"
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:17.734 --> 00:08:20.601
-I'm going to do something.
My own.

00:08:20.601 --> 00:08:24.901
-Recommended it to people.
I love good prosecco and vodka.

00:08:24.901 --> 00:08:27.534
And I was recommending it
to people

00:08:27.534 --> 00:08:29.968
and I put it in the show,
and people were like,

00:08:29.968 --> 00:08:31.400
"Oh, I'm drinking this
because of you."

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:32.801
So I was like, "If they're
going to drink it because of me,

00:08:32.801 --> 00:08:35.167
I want it to be from me,"
so Viarae was born.

00:08:35.167 --> 00:08:37.767
-Good for you. See?
This is a trailblazer.

00:08:37.767 --> 00:08:39.334
This is what I'm talking about.

00:08:39.334 --> 00:08:41.400
You are --
We have some here tonight.

00:08:41.400 --> 00:08:42.601
We're going to do
a little toast.

00:08:42.601 --> 00:08:44.000
We actually got some
for The Roots, as well.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:46.133
-Come on, Roots.
-Roots, you guys got some.

00:08:46.133 --> 00:08:48.100
-Cheers.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:48.100 --> 00:08:49.534
-Cheers to you guys.
Cheers to The Roots.

00:08:49.534 --> 00:08:50.567
-Cheers.
-Cheers to you, Issa Rae.

00:08:50.567 --> 00:08:51.734
-Cheers, Jimmy.
Thank you so much.

00:08:51.734 --> 00:08:52.734
-We love you.
Come back whenever you want.

00:08:52.734 --> 00:08:53.801
Issa Rae.

00:08:53.801 --> 00:08:57.033
Her new prosecco, Viarae,
is available now.

00:08:57.033 --> 00:08:58.968
More "Tonight Show"
after the break. Stick around.

